<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Tori Fatehpur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1690 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Tori Fatehpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Bundela jagir of Bundelkhand, one of the minor estates recognised by the British in the early 19th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tori Fatehpur was a small estate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>, held by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundela</a> or allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> family. The register dates it to 1690, but its founding is known mainly from local tradition.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The jagirdar ruled a handful of villages. After the British established supremacy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>, the estate was recognised by sanad and supervised through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand-agency">Bundelkhand Agency</a> of Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Little else is recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tori Fatehpur joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a> in 1948 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a> in 1950. Its lands lie in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jhansi-state">Jhansi</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tori-fatehpur-state.jpg" alt="Tori Fatehpur State" width="320" height="172"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tori-Fatehpur_State-2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1690 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tori Fatehpur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tori Fatehpur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1820&amp;focus=tori-fatehpur-state" aria-label="Tori Fatehpur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6776 1242 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tori Fatehpur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7096 1498L7364 1601M7096 1498L7364 1602M7096 1498L7160 1530"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7160 1530h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7096 1498h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7096 1498h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1820&amp;focus=tori-fatehpur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
